Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Here we break up the matrix L into single-row matrices L1 + L2 + L3 + L4 \
containing each  a single row of L, in other words the conjugate of a left \
eigenvector. See the main text for a discussion that the rows of L are not \
the left eigenvectors, but their conjugates. \
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.959179654853194*^9, 3.959179659582118*^9}, {
